✅ How to get Jenkins Initial Admin Password
✔️ Step 1 — Make sure Jenkins container is running

Run:

docker ps


You should see a container named jenkins.
If not running, start it:

docker compose up -d

✔️ Step 2 — Run this command to print the password
Linux / macOS / WSL
docker exec jenkins cat /var/jenkins_home/secrets/initialAdminPassword

Windows CMD
docker exec jenkins cat \var\jenkins_home\secrets\initialAdminPassword

Windows PowerShell
docker exec jenkins cat /var/jenkins_home/secrets/initialAdminPassword


PowerShell uses / — not \.

✔️ After running the command

You will see a long string like:

f3c8b1a41e2f4e1c9d39e6e1d74c59e3


👉 Copy that and paste it in Jenkins unlock screen
http://localhost:8080

⚠️ If you get an error like "No such file or directory"

Run:

docker exec -it jenkins ls /var/jenkins_home/secrets


You should see the file:

initialAdminPassword


If it is not there, Jenkins might still be starting.
Wait 1–2 minutes and try again.

⚠️ If container name is not "jenkins"

Run:

docker ps


Find the actual container name or ID (example: jenkins_jenkins_1).

Then run:

docker exec <container_name> cat /var/jenkins_home/secrets/initialAdminPassword


Example:

docker exec jenkins_jenkins_1 cat /var/jenkins_home/secrets/initialAdminPa
